            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous origin of circumflex artery from right sinus of Valsalva: a rare cause of non-ST elevation syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e105-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case with anomalous origin of the left circumflex artery from the right coronary artery ostium, which caused a non-ST elevation coronary syndrome. A review of the literature indicates this to be an extremely rare case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
